  "delivered_messages_sha256": "03608f690877809d6853bad0482bb769ba9f1eb38d88bf01e6bea392d628d0dc",
  "raw_text": "No. A past “production restored” note only documents that a restore occurred at that time. It does not prove that today’s empty local database is the same database or environment.\n\nTo establish continuity, verify evidence such as:\n\n- Database/server instance identity and connection string\n- Restore timestamp and backup identifier\n- Environment or container lifecycle/recreation history\n- Database creation/reset logs or migration history\n- Current schema, row counts, and known restored records\n- Snapshots, checksums, or audit logs\n\nAbsent that evidence, the empty database could be a different instance, a later reset, or a recreated local environment.",
